# Per-session substrate residue. These are written by tooling into the repo and
# are meaningless outside the session that wrote them. Left untracked, every pane
# in the fleet carries a permanently dirty `git status` — and a tree that is
# always dirty is how a real uncommitted change gets missed.
.claude/nf-session-seen-*.flag
prompts/.claude/nf-session-seen-*.flag

# Local analysis cache, regenerated on demand.
.planning/

# Per-agent git worktrees (see #19). Daintree/Claude place them inside the repo,
# so without this every worktree dirties `git status` in every other pane.
.claude/worktrees/
